ADDITIONAL PERMISSION UNDER AGPL-3.0 SECTION 7

    As an additional permission under section 7, you are allowed to
    distribute this software through an app store, even if that store has
    restrictive terms and conditions that are incompatible with the AGPL,
    provided that the source is also available under the AGPL, with or
    without this permission, through a channel without those restrictive
    terms and conditions.

This permission exists because the App Store terms of service impose usage
restrictions that the AGPL forbids a distributor from adding. Without it,
Saadiah could not lawfully be published there. Distribution through
F-Droid and from the project's own release page is, and will remain,
free of any such restriction.

